  "id": "q-81205",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "If $U=\\{-20,-18,-16,-14,…,20\\}$ is the universal set and $A=\\{-20,-16,-12,-8,…,20\\},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$",
      "original_html_sha256": "0773e5135f4f5a3f02bde3305aa69adfb505d8a5a2b28ac547480d954be3d79c",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071504/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/0773e5135f4f5a3f02bde3305aa69adfb505d8a5a2b28ac547480d954be3d79c.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the even integers $-20$ through $20,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $4$ from $-20$ through $20.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the even integers from $-18$ through $18$ that are not multiples of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}=\\{-18,-14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14,18\\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "06604a7af5ad6ce58d63e9106040715fe9ea6fcc27f8ce92cdd35ca8dd148eac",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
